theorem an-instance-asking-the-fewest-conditions
  note        Both parts of the line at x := a give a + 0 = a, the first only
              where a > 0: the part asking nothing is the one taken.
  assume (for all x ∈ ℝ, if x > 0 then x + 0 = x) and (for all x ∈ ℝ, x + 0 = x)   (H1)
  let a ∈ ℝ                                                           (H2)
  then a + 0 = a

1.  a + 0 = a
    instantiate x := a in H1, from H2
